* Next implementation work
** Recurring rounds
*** Save the scheduling channel in guild settings. Use the configured first
    survey date, launch time, timezone, and weekly or biweekly cadence.
*** Reuse one launch workflow for the local scheduler, the eventual production
    scheduler, and a manual trigger. Let admins force a launch without consuming
    the scheduled occurrence.
** Session messages and voting
*** Make the suggestion form say to browse =/activity history= outside the form.
    When a member leaves the field blank, show their current suggestion in the
    confirmation instead of saying it was unchanged.

* Manual Discord validation
** Use multiple legitimate, manually operated accounts in the private server.
** Round lifecycle and permissions
*** Run =/round close= before the deadline and check the result and any activity
    poll appear in the original channel. A second close should find no open
    round. Check low turnout cancellation and that creating a new round cancels
    the previous open one.
*** Use =/round set-event-date= on a finalized latest round and check that
    =/round status= shows the new date and original winning slot. Check that an
    invalid date or an open or cancelled latest round is rejected.
*** Check that members without Manage Server cannot use either wipe command
    and see whether Discord hides those commands from them.
** Venue and hosting
*** Read the default in-person preference, save Virtual, and confirm it reads
    back privately. Create rounds before and after changing saved preferences.
    Confirm each round keeps its opening preferences, starts with no host, and
    that =/round wipe= preserves member preferences.
*** Check that reopening a form preselects the last round choice. On flexible
    rounds, volunteer using the venue picker, then switch to Virtual and confirm
    the offer is withdrawn. Check that in-person-only rounds ask about hosting
    directly.
*** With an eligible host, check that only virtual preferences from the winning
    slot affect the result. Check that the next round after a virtual session
    opens in person only.
    Confirm the first-time or least recent eligible host wins, a volunteer who
    missed the winning slot is excluded, and no eligible host means a virtual
    fallback even on an in-person-only round.
** Activity results and reminders
*** Change a ballot by replacing and removing choices. Confirm the tally uses
    the latest ballot and =/round status= lists the voter once. After the vote
    lock is implemented, confirm changes are rejected after the complete post.
*** Move the latest finalized session to tomorrow with =/round set-event-date=.
    Confirm it stays quiet before noon in the guild's timezone, then posts one
    reminder using the new date. Cover sessions with and without activity polls
    and a session with a newer round open. Leave a ballot missing to check the partial
    totals in the reminder, then submit the last ballot and check that one
    complete totals post follows.
*** confirm can't submit ballot changes after the complete activity totals are posted or event is over

* Maintenance and rollout
** Collect user-facing messages in one place for editing. Refine their wording
   and appearance, including possible Pooky-themed messages.
** Simplify file organization and separate validation from workflow logic
   where it helps readability. Revisit round, poll, and session terminology,
   with session as the preferred user-facing term.
** Review free text validation and keep secrets out of logs and captures.
** Push the code to GitHub. Validate the full workflow in the private server
   before deploying to the real server.

* Optional follow-ups
** Add an admin =/activity delete= command for unwanted or duplicate activities.
   Explore consolidating similar names, possibly with AI assistance.
** Consider letting members retract an activity ballot completely.
** Consider reminder messages before an availability deadline.
** Generalize setup and rollout for multiple independent Discord servers.
** Add unit tests based on the private-server checklist. Consider capturing
   Discord interactions for local replay.
** Explore agent passthrough for simplifying the code.
** Write =AGENTS.md= to document preferred development practices.
